	(text "USB to RS485"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.748 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 7.62 7.62)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1ccdcbf6-df04-4cfe-94bd-8afaf661c39f")
	)
	(text "Notes\n\n1.	USB to TTY IC (FT231XS)\n	-	VCC is powered by a 3V3 input. Pin 10 (3V3OUT hence has to be powered by 3V3)\n	-	3V3 power means that logic level is 3V3\n	-	FT231XS is chosen since FTDI chips are easy to source and well supported. FT231XS is used instead of the older FT232RL since FT232RL is EOL\n	-	TXDEN (CBUS0) does not need to be wired since THV1406 has auto-direction detection\n	-	8mA nominal power consumption\n2.	UART TTY to RS485 IC (THVD1406)\n	-	~{RE} and ~{SHDN} are tied together to logic high for auto-direction detection\n	-	logic low: 0.2V\n	-	logic high: Vcc - 0.2V = 3.1V\n	-	1.7mA typical power consumption"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8161d7d5-cba2-45f9-9d34-8f151a0583cb")
	)
